{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Under thirty seconds remain and no new evidence is possible, so this references the retained draft. The audit closed with all necessary gaps resolved and no open questions: the snapshot is unmodified upstream etcd-raft v3.7.0 at commit b867cf13. Two sourced defects are asserted with retained executions. Read-index retry growth: per-request, context-blind admission accumulates same-context retries as queued or unconfirmed entries with no library-side bound and no reclamation during the process lifetime, released later as a burst of one admission plus one heartbeat per entry; measured across the queued path and its retention across deposition, the admitted path, the release burst, a CheckQuorum control that closes the growth window at step-down while keeping the state, a byte measurement of caller payload of 262144 bytes for 64 requests with 4 KiB contexts in 64 distinct buffers, and a real isolated-leader network run where 32 requests gave confirmed zero and 64 heartbeats, correcting the amplification to one heartbeat per peer per retry. Configuration change: with a joint configuration and no change pending unapplied, an empty ConfChangeV2 whose transition is not Auto passes propose-time validation as an EntryConfChangeV2, commits in a real three-node network, and panics the application in ApplyConfChange with config is already joint, while the Auto form remains the working control and the pending-conf guard is a precondition. Four further threads are explained or refuted with boundaries stated: readOnly ack validation out of contract, queued read requests kept fresh across term changes, the StateSnapshot repair duty with both exits observed, and proposer eligibility of removed members resting with the caller under the documented MsgProp contract.\"}"}}
